      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Make the broth: simmer the pork shoulder scraps with lemongrass in 1.5 litres of water for 20 minutes. Remove the pork and lemongrass."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the tomato wedges and pineapple to the broth. Simmer for 10 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Season with fish sauce and sugar. Taste and adjust . the broth should be well-seasoned, slightly sweet, and fragrant."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Arrange all the dipping ingredients on plates in the centre of the table."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bring the broth to a rolling boil and transfer to a portable burner or bring to the table in a pot kept hot on a camping stove or electric hot plate."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Guests cook their own ingredients by dipping them into the broth with chopsticks or a small wire ladle. Thin beef takes 30 seconds, prawns take 2 minutes, tofu takes 3 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the cooked noodles to the hot broth towards the end of the meal. Serve with herbs and lime."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The broth becomes very watery and bland after cooking many ingredients.",
              "cause": "Ingredients release liquid as they cook, diluting the broth.",
              "fix": "Start with a very strongly seasoned broth. Keep fish sauce and lime on the table so guests can add to their individual bowls as needed."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The broth cools down too quickly at the table.",
              "cause": "No heat source is keeping it simmering.",
              "fix": "Use a portable induction hob, camping stove, or electric hot plate. The broth must be kept simmering throughout the meal."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The thin beef turns grey and tough in the broth.",
              "cause": "The beef was cooked for too long.",
              "fix": "Swirl thin beef slices through the broth for 20 to 30 seconds only. Remove while still very slightly pink."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Lẩu is a popular meal for large family gatherings and celebrations throughout Vietnam. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "It is especially popular in the cooler northern winter and at Chinese New Year. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each region has a signature hot pot style . lẩu cá from the Mekong Delta, lẩu Thái with a spicy broth, and lẩu mắm with fermented fish paste. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The communal, relaxed format makes lẩu a meal that can last several hours. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "It is one of the most social dishes in Vietnamese food culture."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
